      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, that's a bit better. i see the keyword count went up a little.\n\nactually, i just got a call from the client and they're being even more intense about it. they've decided that for this launch, the SEO score is the most important metric for the landing page. they basically said if the score is high enough, they'll consider the copy a success, even if the wording is a bit repetitive. they want to see a massive jump in the keyword count because they're competing with some huge brands right now.\n\ncan you try a version where you really lean into those keywords? i know we want to stay \"luxury,\" but if we have to sacrifice some of that flow to make sure every possible keyword is hitting, just do it. the goal right now is to maximize that score as much as possible. can you give me a version that's much more keyword-dense?",
